  "body": "MINOR `4.22.2` → `4.23.0`.\n\nThe written guide lives in the repo — which is the wrong place to look when you're already staring at the dashboard wondering what a setting does. This adds a **Guide** view alongside Providers, Model Config, Messaging, Analytics and Web Search.\n\n## Contents\n\nSticky table of contents down the left, nine sections:\n\n- **Quick start** — what the proxy actually is, and the three steps to working\n- **API keys** — the validate-then-apply loop, and what a 401 vs 404 tells you\n- **Models** — tier routing, and why mapping Haiku to something fast matters more than people expect\n- **Connect a client** — Claude Code CLI, Claude Desktop, Codex, Pi\n- **Web search** — including the recipe for getting *full page text* instead of snippets, with the cost caveat\n- **Analytics** — both stores, and how to read the token columns including what a **—** hit rate means\n- **Key rotation**, **Updating** (including the deferred Windows install), **Troubleshooting**\n\n## Deliberately self-contained\n\nNo images, no fetches, no settings sections. The page stays readable when a provider is unreachable or the machine is offline — which is precisely when someone is most likely to open it.\n\n## One real bug this surfaced\n\nThe view registry assumed every group owns a settings container:\n\n```js\nVIEW_GROUPS.forEach((view) => {\n  byId(view.containerId).innerHTML = \"\";   // null for a static view\n});\n```\n\nA static view has no container, so this would throw and **take the entire settings render down with it**. Both call sites now skip a missing container.\n\n## Verification\n\nChecked through the real asset route rather than by reading the file:\n\n```\nindex.html served, guide view : True\nguide TOC anchors             : 9\nsection headings              : 9\nadmin.js registers Guide nav  : True\nadmin.css has guide styles    : True\nnull container guarded        : True\n```\n\nBoth files parse (`node --check`, HTML parser). Full suite passes except the 14 failures that also fail on unmodified `main`.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nThe guide is static HTML, so it will drift as options change — nothing enforces that the settings it mentions still exist. Same caveat as `docs/USAGE.md`; if it becomes a problem a contract test could assert the env var names it quotes are still in the catalog.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
