    },
    "message": "feat(admin): add an in-dashboard Guide page\n\nThe written guide lives in the repository, which is the wrong place to look\nwhen you are already staring at the dashboard wondering what a setting does.\nThis adds a Guide view alongside Providers, Model Config, Messaging, Analytics\nand Web Search.\n\nContent is static HTML with a sticky table of contents: quick start, adding and\nvalidating keys and what a 401 versus a 404 actually tells you, model tiers and\nwhy mapping Haiku to something fast matters more than people expect, connecting\nClaude Code, Claude Desktop, Codex and Pi, web search including the recipe for\ngetting full page text rather than snippets, both analytics stores and how to\nread the token columns, key rotation, the deferred Windows update, and\ntroubleshooting.\n\nDeliberately self-contained: no images, no fetches, no settings sections. The\npage stays readable when a provider is unreachable or the machine is offline,\nwhich is exactly when someone is most likely to open it.\n\nThe view registry assumed every group owns a settings container and called\nbyId(view.containerId).innerHTML on each one. A static view has none, so both\ncall sites now skip a missing container -- without that guard a null container\nwould throw and take the whole settings render down with it.\n\nVerified through the real asset route: the served index.html carries the view\nwith nine sections and nine matching anchors, admin.js registers the nav entry,\nthe stylesheet ships, and both files parse.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
